NAME "Buffer redstone counter (experimental)"

-- Connect three resource buffers to the manager and label them donor, counter,
-- and sink. Put a comparator against counter, pointing away from the buffer.
-- Seed donor with 2 units; leave counter and sink empty. For a developer world:
-- /setblock <x> <y> <z> sfm:buffer{redstone:2}
-- Place the other two with /setblock <x> <y> <z> sfm:buffer
-- Buffer items/recipes are still experimental; commands can place the block.

EVERY 20 TICKS DO
    IF donor HAS GT 0 redstone:: THEN
        INPUT 1 redstone:: FROM donor
        OUTPUT redstone:: TO counter
    ELSE
        INPUT 1 redstone:: FROM counter
        OUTPUT redstone:: TO sink
    END
END

-- Counter follows 0 -> 1 -> 2 -> 1 -> 0, then stays at 0.
-- Transfers conserve stored units. World signals cannot supply or accept units.
-- HAS reads the exact stored count, including quantities above 15.
-- A comparator emits min(count, 15); an empty counter emits 0.
-- Redstone counts persist when the world is saved and loaded.
-- redstone:: units are separate from minecraft:redstone items.
